   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Talking about the future with the present tense",
     "texto": [
      "As in English, German uses the **present tense** with a time word to talk about plans: **Morgen besuche ich meine Eltern** (tomorrow I'm visiting my parents). No future tense is needed.",
      "Future words: **morgen** (tomorrow), **heute Abend** (tonight), **am Wochenende**, **nächste Woche** (next week).",
      "Remember: if you start with the time expression, the verb stays in second place and the subject goes after it."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Inviting",
     "texto": [
      "**Möchtest du kommen?** (would you like to come?) or **Kommst du mit?** (are you coming along?).",
      "To accept: **Gern!** or **Sehr gern!** (with pleasure!). To decline: **Leider kann ich nicht** (unfortunately I can't).",
      "To arrange to meet: **Treffen wir uns um acht?** (shall we meet at eight?).",
      "**Gute Idee!** = good idea!"
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
